{"name":"Harley Davidson Orange","hex":"#c93413","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"orange","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An evergreen tree of the genus Citrus such as Citrus sinensis which yields oranges (the fruit).","Any round citrus fruit with a yellow-red colour when ripe and a sour-sweet taste; the fruit of the orange tree.\n Specifically, a sweet orange or Citrus sinensis."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Having the colour of the fruit of an orange tree; yellowred; reddish-yellow."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/orange"}],"entries":[{"title":"Harley-Davidson","blocks":[{"text":"Harley-Davidson, Inc. is an American motorcycle manufacturer and lifestyle brand headquartered in Milwaukee, Wisconsin. Founded in 1903, it is one of two major American motorcycle manufacturers to survive the Great Depression along with its historical rival, Indian Motorcycle Company. The company has survived numerous ownership arrangements, subsidiary arrangements, periods of poor economic health and product quality, and intense global competition to become an iconic brand widely known for its loyal following. There are owner clubs and events worldwide, as well as a company-sponsored, brand-focused museum."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bb/Harley_Davidson_orange_logo.svg/330px-Harley_Davidson_orange_logo.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Harley-Davidson","wikidata":"Q192814"},{"title":"Orange (colour)","blocks":[{"text":"Orange is the colour between yellow and red on the spectrum of visible light. The human eyes perceive orange when observing light with a dominant wavelength between roughly 585 and 620 nanometres. In traditional colour theory, it is a secondary colour of pigments, produced by mixing yellow and red. In the RGB colour model, it is a tertiary colour. It is named after the fruit of the same name."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d8/Delicatearch.png/330px-Delicatearch.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Orange_(colour)","wikidata":"Q39338"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8b/Harley-Davidson_Motorcycle_Factory_Building_original_site.jpg/500px-Harley-Davidson_Motorcycle_Factory_Building_original_site.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8b/Harley-Davidson_Motorcycle_Factory_Building_original_site.jpg/1280px-Harley-Davidson_Motorcycle_Factory_Building_original_site.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8b/Harley-Davidson_Motorcycle_Factory_Building_original_site.jpg/500px-Harley-Davidson_Motorcycle_Factory_Building_original_site.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AHarley-Davidson_Motorcycle_Factory_Building_original_site.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/51/Founders_of_Harley-Davidson_The_North_Shore_Bulletin_Dec_1920.jpg/500px-Founders_of_Harley-Davidson_The_North_Shore_Bulletin_Dec_1920.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/51/Founders_of_Harley-Davidson_The_North_Shore_Bulletin_Dec_1920.jpg/500px-Founders_of_Harley-Davidson_The_North_Shore_Bulletin_Dec_1920.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"From left: William A. Davidson, Walter Davidson Sr., Arthur Davidson and William S. Harley","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AFounders_of_Harley-Davidson_The_North_Shore_Bulletin_Dec_1920.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commo